WEBVTT

00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:12,580
I have some kind of infection in my body that I cannot get rid of.

00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:18,100
I can't fix the structural wall of my chest back.

00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:21,700
I believe it originated in the stomach, possibly H. Pylora,

00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:25,580
Xantivionic resistant affects my brain,

00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:27,660
eyesight, muscles, all my joints.

00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:32,540
I'm unable to get IV antibiotic therapy.

00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:35,620
So I don't know where the question is of that,

00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:39,300
except maybe what could this possibly be?

00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:44,420
So when you have an antibiotic-resistant infection,

00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:46,540
it certainly could be a bacteria

00:00:46,540 --> 00:00:49,060
that you're just not getting the right antibiotic.

00:00:49,060 --> 00:00:53,220
So getting whatever affected area cultured

00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:56,300
contested for what is going to be the best antibiotic

00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:59,340
if it is a bacteria is the right thing to do

00:00:59,340 --> 00:01:01,740
if you have a chronic infection.

00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:04,700
The other thing, possibility is that it's not a bacteria.

00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:06,380
So if it's not a bacteria,

00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:08,540
then antibiotics aren't going to help at all.

00:01:08,540 --> 00:01:13,540
So if you're trying to take care of some chronic viral infection

00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:16,620
with an antibiotic, it's not going to work.

00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:18,540
Chronic infections are real.

00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:22,900
You can't have bacteria, viruses, parasites, different fungi

00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:28,740
that are resistant to your immune system's ability to kill them

00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:30,500
for all sorts of different reasons.

00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:34,340
On our chronic Lyme course, I go into details

00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:36,980
on the different reasons that that happens.

00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:40,900
These different organisms have the ability to hide

00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:43,220
within your normal microbiota.

00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:46,420
They have the ability to create walls around them

00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:49,780
so that your immune system can't kill it.

00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:52,060
And worse, they have the ability,

00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:54,140
sometimes to go intracellular.

00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:56,700
So if they go inside of a cell,

00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:58,900
then your immune system isn't going to kill

00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:01,460
something your immune system doesn't go inside the cell.

00:02:01,460 --> 00:02:05,300
So if they're hiding within cells and they're replicating

00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:07,700
and they're going outside of cells and making you sick

00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:10,540
and that operation continues,

00:02:10,540 --> 00:02:12,700
yeah, you could have what's called a chronic infection.

00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:16,980
So it could be bacterial, it could be viral.

00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:21,060
There's tests that you could do to find out.

00:02:21,060 --> 00:02:23,980
There is, if you know what's a pathogen,

00:02:23,980 --> 00:02:27,220
running a pathogen antibody array,

00:02:27,220 --> 00:02:30,700
which is a Cyrex array 12, I think it is,

00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:33,940
can be helpful to know what you're dealing with.

00:02:34,940 --> 00:02:37,820
I will say that there's people that think

00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:40,860
that they may have a chronic pathogen,

00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:44,140
but really they just have a chronic autoimmune disease

00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:46,260
that has yet to be diagnosed.

00:02:46,260 --> 00:02:49,820
So getting proper workup is really important.

00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:54,060
Running antibody tests for self tissue is important

00:02:54,940 --> 00:02:58,260
to just rule things out because it may not,

00:02:58,260 --> 00:03:01,860
